[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Design the architecture for a URL shortener that handles 10k requests a second, as a Markdown file\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[37.468, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/url-shortener-architecture.md)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[42.2, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I wrote the architecture to `<workspace>/url-shortener-architecture.md`. I haven't run or load-tested\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  anything. The sizing numbers are back-of-envelope estimates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Load model:** I assumed a 100:1 read-to-write ratio. That gives about 9.9k redirects/s and about 100\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  creates/s, which is a modest load.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Read path:** requests go through the CDN, then the redirect service, then an in-process cache, then\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Redis, then the database. I'd expect a cache hit rate above 95%.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Separate services:** redirect and create run as separate services, so a write spike can't slow\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  redirects.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Short codes:** each create instance takes a block of 10,000 IDs from a central counter and hands them\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  out locally. The IDs are scrambled before base62 encoding so codes can't be guessed in sequence.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Storage:** I chose a replicated key-value store, since the only access pattern is lookup by code.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Sharded Postgres is listed as an alternative.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Analytics:** click events go through Kafka to ClickHouse and are never part of the redirect request.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The document also covers an API sketch, capacity sizing, failure handling, abuse prevention, monitoring, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a table of the main trade-offs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Two choices you might want to change. I defaulted to a 302 redirect with a 60-second cache lifetime, which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  keeps click analytics and link deletion working at the cost of some caching. I also left the choice between\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a key-value store and sharded Postgres open, because either handles this load.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
