[876.4, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The final document passes the outside check I built, 94 of 94, including all the links. I saved it to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/steps/6/`. The check script is `.ambition/work/doc_check.py`, and it is not part of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  deliverable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the check does:** it uses no model. It re-runs every embedded script against its printed output. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  also cross-checks the prose figures against that output, validates section and appendix references and table\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  shape, fetches every cited link, and scans for stale claims. It then scores the document against the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  original ask and each promise in the restatement. It also checks that nothing the first version offered has\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  been lost, by searching for 28 capability terms.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What it caught before the cold read**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - One script's printed output didn't match what the script prints: A3 claimed \"collisions: 0, all\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  invertible\" and the script doesn't print that. A6's table also had the wrong indentation. I regenerated both\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  from real runs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Meta wording that reviewers wouldn't understand: \"my first draft\" appeared in the intro and the abuse\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  table. The changes table is now \"Revision notes\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Two of the check's own bugs: it was stripping leading spaces and over-flagging the revision table. I fixed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  those too.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version, same check:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The first version fails 8 of the promises (summary and diagram up front, decision records, derivations,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  marked assumptions, cache and database failure cases, embedded scripts, sources, abuse analysis). The final\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  passes all of them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The check found nothing the first version had that the final lacks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The final is longer (601 lines vs about 250), and most of the growth is the appendices.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Cold read:** I read the whole body as a reviewer meeting it for the first time and found six issues. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fixed them:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the \"CPU > 60%\" autoscale trigger was explained but never stated;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the 11-character unlisted tier appeared in D2 but not in the create API;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - there was no failure row for the scanner being down;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - one unsourced claim (\"default of a few dozen\");\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - an unnumbered section between 1 and 2;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the opening line overclaimed that every number was derived.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Not checked:** I haven't rendered the Markdown in a viewer, so layout is judged from the raw text only. No\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real people reviewed it. The check can't tell whether the design is right, only that the document's numbers,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  references and promises are consistent with the evidence I gathered.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course:** none. The cold read was the part that added the most.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
