[1207.515, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Ask:** an architecture for a 10k req/s URL shortener, as a Markdown file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Became:** a design-review document with:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - a summary and one diagram;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - decision records, each with rejected alternatives and what would flip the decision;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - numbers that show their working, backed by scripts and sources;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - failure modes, an attack table and an availability budget;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - a stretch section for 100k req/s;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - a decisions table with owners and dates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better on every part of the ask:** 8 of the promises in the restatement fail on the first version and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  pass now. The check found nothing the first version offered that the final lacks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gave up:** the \"possible extensions\" list, which didn't serve the review.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cost:** the document is longer (675 lines vs about 250), mostly from the appendices.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where it changed the design:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The first draft's \">95% cache hit rate\" didn't survive the simulation or the real trace.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Random codes replaced the ID service.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Redis shrank to one primary plus a replica.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check:** `check_architecture.py` passed 112 of 112 with `--run --links` and the first version as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  baseline, and 43 of 43 without `--run`. It re-runs the 8 embedded scripts and compares each with its printed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  output. It also checks the prose figures against that output, fetches every cited link, and checks\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  structure, cross-references and tables. It confirms no process story remains and that every decision and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  next check has an owner and date. It can't judge whether the design is right. I haven't rendered the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Markdown in a viewer, and no real people reviewed it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch:** 100k req/s, 10× the brief.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Result:** the same architecture gets there, with a changed configuration.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Breaks first:** DynamoDB's default 40k read-unit quota (100% of reads would use 124% of it).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Also needed:** Redis in three shards, and 12–34 redirect instances.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Unmeasured:** instance throughput beyond about 15k req/s, because this laptop saturated.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in** (in `<workspace>`)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `check_architecture.py`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `CLAUDE.md`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `.claude/commands/check-architecture.md`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  To rerun, use `python3 -I check_architecture.py url-shortener-architecture.md --run --links`, or `/check-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  architecture`. The `--run` option needs the two input files named in Appendix A, under `.ambition/data/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Step snapshots are in `.ambition/steps/2` through `8`, and the first version is in `.ambition/first`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made:** none on your behalf; you answered each question.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions left** (full table with owners and dates in Section 9). The most urgent:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Link privacy (decide by 2026-11-27).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Options:** 7 characters for all, 7 public plus 11 unlisted, or 11 for all.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **For and against:** shortest URLs against about 736k enumerable live links a day, against four extra\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  characters everywhere.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Pick:** 7 public plus 11 unlisted.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Datastore (2026-11-27).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Options:** DynamoDB, Cassandra/Scylla, or sharded Postgres.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **For and against:** managed but quota-bound and AWS-tied, against self-run but quota-free, against SQL\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tooling but strained by 2.6–7.8 TB.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Pick:** managed key-value store.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Redirect status (2026-11-20).**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Options:** 302 with a 60 s `max-age`, 301, or an uncached 302.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **For and against:** 302 with `max-age` keeps analytics and a roughly 60 s takedown; 301 is cheapest\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  but makes clicks and takedowns invisible; uncached 302 is exact but gets no CDN relief.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Pick:** 302 with `max-age=60`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The owners are proposed roles, not named people.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
